Sam Ortiz: Quick PR to clarify 429/timeouts entry in the troubleshooting page. Need: one compact JS snippet that respects Retry-After and falls back; a 2-line migration note; fix one stale link. @Lina can you review?

Lina Morales: Happy to. Keep the snippet under 12 lines. Also normalize term to 'context trim' in the copy.

Sam Ortiz: Draft JS snippet: 
```js
async function generateSafe(client, prompt) {
  try { return await client.text.generate({ model: 'redwood-1', prompt }); }
  catch (err) {
    if (err.status === 429) {
      const wait = (parseInt(err.headers?.['Retry-After']||'1')*1000);
      await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, wait));
      return await client.text.generate({ model: 'redwood-1-small', prompt });
    }
    if (err.name === 'TimeoutError') return await client.text.generate({ model: 'redwood-1-small', prompt });
    throw err;
  }
}
```

Lina Morales: Nice and concise. Migration blurb suggestion: 'Honor Retry-After, prefer backoff, and route canary traffic when changing model variants. Confirm prefix caching to reduce token volume.'

DocsBot: CI: docs-lint OK. Linkcheck: /old/ops -> /docs/optimizations/batching redirect. Branch: sam/errref-fix.

Eli Z.: Ran quick stress: 120rps for 20s showed ~8% 429s; local harness using fallback cleared visible errors. Looks good to merge once link updated.

